@startuml deployment-diagram
title Diagrama de Despliegue - Gastos Personales

skinparam linetype ortho
top to bottom direction

actor "Usuario" as user

cloud "Cloudflare\n(Tunnel)" as cf
cloud "API Externa\n(tipo de cambio)" as fx

node "PC Local" as pc {
    node "Docker Engine" as docker {

        node "Frontend Container" as fec {
            artifact "gastos-frontend\n(Angular + Nginx)" as fe
        }

        node "Backend Container" as bec {
            artifact "gastos-backend.jar\n(Spring Boot)" as be
        }

        node "MySQL Container" as dbc {
            database "MySQL 8.4" as db
            artifact "mysql-data\n(volumen)" as data
        }
    }
}

user --> cf : HTTPS
cf --> fe : túnel -> :80
fe --> be : REST (/api)
be --> db : JDBC
db --> data : persistencia
be --> fx : HTTPS

legend bottom
El acceso público se realiza mediante un túnel de Cloudflare, evitando exponer
puertos en el router o usar una IP pública. El frontend (Angular sobre Nginx)
consume servicios REST del backend (Spring Boot), que persiste en MySQL y consulta
el tipo de cambio en una API externa. Todo corre en contenedores Docker en la PC.
endlegend

@enduml
